cealed with potential for multiple chows and pairs. Discarding B7 maintains the T4-T5-T6 chow and avoids giving others a key tile for a Chow with B8.]\nReason: [B7 is part of a Chow with B8 (already in a Pung by the next player), but discarding it safely allows keeping the T4-T5-T6 chow intact. Winds (F2/F3) are less critical for a concealed hand aiming for All Chows (2 points) and Fully Concealed Hand (4 points).]\nAnswer: Play B7"}
